==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|brjóst}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*breustą}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*bʰrews-||to swell}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/prjoust/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|oust|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|brjósts|brjóst}}

# one of a woman's [[breast]]s
# [[breast]] ([[chest]])
# {{lb|is|chiefly|poetic}} [[breast]] (a person's seat of [[emotion]])
# the front of something

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s|br|jó|st}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|woman's breast}} {{l|is|bobbingur}} {{qualifier|colloquial, somewhat offensive}}
* {{sense|chest}} {{l|is|bringa}}
* {{sense|seat of emotion}} {{l|is|hjarta}} (literally "heart")

====Derived terms====
